{
  "dom_id": "step-e4646",
  "name": "Example: Identifying the Reflection of a Sine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/cee9fbb5ec7f781ed591a9817f6443610ec1558b04297688f0fe793e2b8a761d.png)\n\nThe graph above represents a transformed sine curve. What is the equation of the graph?",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/bb9f9e2111d71068c98a693977f73ce712c8b7f77cebeebb58db936f72e74fe7.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\sin x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $8$ to give $y=-8\\sin x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-8\\sin x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
